  "chapter_note": "This chapter contains NO cosmological substrate. It is wholly a pastoral-pedagogical kephalaion about Wisdom as transmitted teaching — why proclaiming Wisdom produces more joy than holding her in the heart, and why some hearers receive her while others do not. The teaching method uses correspondential comparison (child in womb, fire hidden in wood) but the comparisons map Wisdom→natural phenomena to illustrate a pedagogical/experiential point — not cosmic realm→cosmic realm. There are no cosmic hierarchies, no Five Sons, no kings, no zoomorphic mapping. The whole chapter is dialogue-framed hortatory/parabolic application addressing the editor's pastoral concerns about teaching reception. Classified entirely as apostolic_dialogue (frame formulae) and hortatory_application (parabolic pastoral content).",
